IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): Part VIII "Self-employed Persons Engaged in Fishing" (s 153), Part VIII.1 "Alternate
-- Access to Special Benefits" (s 153.1), Part VIII.2 "Regulations -- Provincial Plans" (s 153.2) and Part VIII.3 "Interim Orders"
-- (ss 153.3 and 153.4). Piece ei4. Layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- These Parts are almost wholly powers to make regulations or orders; they are not encoded as rules (see the coverage table: each
-- is `inert` with the reason). What they decide for a person is encoded here: the sitting day of s 153(9); the class of people the
-- alternate-access scheme is for and the people it may not reach (s 153.1(1) and (3)); and, for an interim order, when it may be made,
-- when it ends, and when it prevails over the Act (s 153.3(2) to (4), (7), (8), (9)).
-- Conventions as in ei4-part-vi-review.l4. The fishing regulations (s 153) are a separate instrument that is not among the inputs; the
-- alternate-access regulations (s 153.1) are Part VI of the Regulations (piece er6); the Regulations' provincial-plan provisions (Part III.1,
-- piece er4) deal with the subject of s 153.2, and the deposited text does not say they were made under it.
-- This range holds no enactment date, assent date or commencement rule: the Act's coming into force is s 190 (piece ei6). The two
-- dates it does carry are the 30 September 2020 end of the power to make interim orders (s 153.3(9)) and, in Part VII, 30 June 1996.

§ `Part VIII -- Self-employed Persons Engaged in Fishing`

§§ `s 153(9) Definition of sitting day`

-- src:2709 | (9) For the purpose of this section, sitting day means a day on which the House of Commons is sitting.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153(9) (src:2709)
GIVEN `the House of Commons is sitting on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153(9) the day is a sitting day` IF
    `the House of Commons is sitting on the day`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- Alternate Access to Special Benefits`

§§ `s 153.1(1) and (3) The people the scheme is for, and the people it may not reach`

-- The class the scheme is made for: an insured person with at least 600 hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period who
-- does not qualify to receive benefits under section 7 (out of range: piece ei1). 600 is the Act's own figure.
-- src:2713 | 153.1 (1) Despite anything in this Act, the Commission shall, with the approval of the Governor in Council, make any regulations it considers necessary respecting the establishment and operation of a scheme to ensure that special benefits are provided to insured persons who have at least 600 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period but who do not qualify to receive benefits under section 7, including regulations
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1(1) (src:2713)
GIVEN `is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `qualifies to receive benefits under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 7 (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` IF
        `is an insured person`
    AND `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` AT LEAST 600
    AND NOT (`qualifies to receive benefits under section 7`)

-- (3): "may not provide special benefits to persons who are subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of
-- insurable employment required to qualify for benefits". TRUE means the bar applies to the person.
-- src:2719 | (3) The scheme established by the regulations may not provide special benefits to persons who are subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1(3) (src:2719)
GIVEN `is subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 7.1 (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1(3) the scheme may not provide special benefits to the person` IF
    `is subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits`

-- The two together: the people the scheme is meant to give special benefits to.
-- src:2713 | 153.1 (1) Despite anything in this Act, the Commission shall, with the approval of the Governor in Council, make any regulations it considers necessary respecting the establishment and operation of a scheme to ensure that special benefits are provided to insured persons who have at least 600 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period but who do not qualify to receive benefits under section 7, including regulations
-- src:2719 | (3) The scheme established by the regulations may not provide special benefits to persons who are subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1(1) and (3) (src:2713) (src:2719)
GIVEN `is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `qualifies to receive benefits under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1 the scheme is meant to give the person special benefits` IF
        `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` `is an insured person` `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` `qualifies to receive benefits under section 7`
    AND NOT (`s 153.1(3) the scheme may not provide special benefits to the person` `is subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits`)

§ `Part VIII.3 -- Interim Orders`

§§ `s 153.3(9) The date the power ends`

-- src:2759 | (9) The power to make an interim order under subsection (1) is not to be exercised after September 30, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(9) (src:2759)
`s 153.3(9) September 30, 2020` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 9 30

§§ `s 153.3(1) to (4) When an interim order may be made`

-- The Minister's power to make an interim order is machinery, but the conditions on it decide whether an order that touches a person
-- was validly made: the purpose (1), no order in respect of Part IV or VII (2), the consent of the Minister of Finance (3), the
-- additional consent of the President of the Treasury Board for Part III (4), and no exercise after 30 September 2020 (9).
-- The Minister's purpose is a fact about the order, so it is an input. The consents are facts.
-- src:2737 | 153.3 (1) The Minister may, for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19), make interim orders that
-- src:2738 | (a) add provisions, including provisions that provide for new benefits, to this Act or any regulation made under this Act;
-- src:2739 | (b) adapt provisions of this Act or any regulation made under this Act; or
-- src:2740 | (c) provide that any provisions of this Act or a regulation made under this Act do not apply in whole or in part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(1) (src:2737-2740)
GIVEN `the order is made for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order adds provisions, adapts provisions, or provides that provisions do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.3(1) the order is an interim order of the kind the Minister may make` IF
        `the order is made for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)`
    AND `the order adds provisions, adapts provisions, or provides that provisions do not apply`

-- src:2742 | (2) An interim order is not to be made under subsection (1) in respect of Part IV or VII or in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of those Parts.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(2) (src:2742)
GIVEN `the order is in respect of Part IV or VII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of Part IV or VII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.3(2) an interim order is not to be made in respect of the matter` IF
       `the order is in respect of Part IV or VII`
    OR `the order is in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of Part IV or VII`

-- src:2744 | (3) An interim order is not to be made under subsection (1) without the consent of the Minister of Finance.
-- src:2745 | Condition precedent — President of the Treasury Board
-- src:2746 | (4) An interim order is not to be made under subsection (1) in respect of Part III or in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of that Part without the additional consent of the President of the Treasury Board.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(3) and (4) (src:2744) (src:2746)
GIVEN `the Minister of Finance has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in respect of Part III or of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of that Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the President of the Treasury Board has additionally consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.3(3) and (4) the consents required for the order have been given` IF
        `the Minister of Finance has consented`
    AND ((NOT (`the order is in respect of Part III or of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of that Part`)) OR `the President of the Treasury Board has additionally consented`)

-- src:2737 | 153.3 (1) The Minister may, for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19), make interim orders that
-- src:2738 | (a) add provisions, including provisions that provide for new benefits, to this Act or any regulation made under this Act;
-- src:2739 | (b) adapt provisions of this Act or any regulation made under this Act; or
-- src:2740 | (c) provide that any provisions of this Act or a regulation made under this Act do not apply in whole or in part.
-- src:2741 | Restriction
-- src:2742 | (2) An interim order is not to be made under subsection (1) in respect of Part IV or VII or in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of those Parts.
-- src:2743 | Condition precedent — Minister of Finance
-- src:2744 | (3) An interim order is not to be made under subsection (1) without the consent of the Minister of Finance.
-- src:2745 | Condition precedent — President of the Treasury Board
-- src:2746 | (4) An interim order is not to be made under subsection (1) in respect of Part III or in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of that Part without the additional consent of the President of the Treasury Board.
-- src:2759 | (9) The power to make an interim order under subsection (1) is not to be exercised after September 30, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(1) to (4) and (9) (src:2737-2746) (src:2759)
GIVEN `the order is made for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order adds provisions, adapts provisions, or provides that provisions do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in respect of Part IV or VII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of Part IV or VII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Finance has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in respect of Part III or of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of that Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the President of the Treasury Board has additionally consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` IF
        `s 153.3(1) the order is an interim order of the kind the Minister may make` `the order is made for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)` `the order adds provisions, adapts provisions, or provides that provisions do not apply`
    AND NOT (`s 153.3(2) an interim order is not to be made in respect of the matter` `the order is in respect of Part IV or VII` `the order is in respect of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of Part IV or VII`)
    AND `s 153.3(3) and (4) the consents required for the order have been given` `the Minister of Finance has consented` `the order is in respect of Part III or of a regulation made under this Act for the purposes of that Part` `the President of the Treasury Board has additionally consented`
    AND `the day on which the order is made` AT MOST `s 153.3(9) September 30, 2020`

§§ `s 153.3(6) to (8) Retroactive effect, cessation, conflict`

-- src:2750 | (6) An interim order made under subsection (1) may, if it so provides, have retroactive effect.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(6) (src:2750)
GIVEN `the interim order provides that it has retroactive effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.3(6) the interim order has retroactive effect` IF
    `the interim order provides that it has retroactive effect`

-- (c) "the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect": strictly after, so a first
-- anniversary that is itself a Saturday gives the following Saturday (fork F-ei4-17). The Saturday that ends the week containing the
-- day after the anniversary is that Saturday.
-- src:2755 | (c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(7)(c) (src:2755)
GIVEN `the day on which the interim order takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` IS
    `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` ((`add years` `the day on which the interim order takes effect` 1) PLUS 1)

-- src:2752 | (7) An interim order made under subsection (1) must contain provisions that cause any provision added under paragraph (1)(a), any adaptation made under paragraph (1)(b) and any non-application provision made under paragraph (1)(c) to cease to apply on the earliest of
-- src:2753 | (a) the day, if any, specified in the interim order,
-- src:2754 | (b) the day on which the interim order is repealed, and
-- src:2755 | (c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(7) (src:2752-2755)
GIVEN firstday IS A DATE
      secondday IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 153.3(7) the earlier of two days` IS
    IF firstday AT MOST secondday THEN firstday ELSE secondday

-- "the earliest of (a) the day, if any, specified in the interim order, (b) the day on which the interim order is repealed, and (c)".
-- A day that does not exist (no day specified, not repealed) takes no part in the choice.
-- src:2752 | (7) An interim order made under subsection (1) must contain provisions that cause any provision added under paragraph (1)(a), any adaptation made under paragraph (1)(b) and any non-application provision made under paragraph (1)(c) to cease to apply on the earliest of
-- src:2753 | (a) the day, if any, specified in the interim order,
-- src:2754 | (b) the day on which the interim order is repealed, and
-- src:2755 | (c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(7) (src:2752-2755)
GIVEN `the day, if any, specified in the interim order` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the interim order is repealed, if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the interim order takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` IS
    `s 153.3(7) the earlier of two days`
        (`s 153.3(7) the earlier of two days`
            (fromMaybe (`s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` `the day on which the interim order takes effect`) `the day, if any, specified in the interim order`)
            (fromMaybe (`s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` `the day on which the interim order takes effect`) `the day on which the interim order is repealed, if it is`))
        (`s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` `the day on which the interim order takes effect`)

-- src:2757 | (8) If an interim order made under subsection (1) or a provision added under paragraph (1)(a) provides that it applies despite any provision of this Act or any regulation made under this Act, the interim order or added provision prevails to the extent that it conflicts with this Act or any regulation made under this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.3(8) (src:2757)
GIVEN `the interim order or added provision provides that it applies despite any provision of this Act or any regulation made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interim order or added provision conflicts with this Act or a regulation made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.3(8) the interim order or added provision prevails to the extent that it conflicts with this Act or a regulation` IF
        `the interim order or added provision provides that it applies despite any provision of this Act or any regulation made under this Act`
    AND `the interim order or added provision conflicts with this Act or a regulation made under this Act`
